# person_org_edges.tsv has two producers that disagree on line terminators:
# build_person_org_graph.py writes CRLF (csv.writer default under newline=""),
# apply_eponym_decisions.py pins lineterminator="\n". Whichever ran last set the
# whole file, so a rebuild showed every line as changed and buried the real diff.
# Pin LF so the diff reflects the actual change. The generator's other three
# outputs stay CRLF -- they have a single producer and no such flapping.
Zylbercweig/organizations/graph/person_org_edges.tsv text eol=lf

# media_manifest.tsv: write_manifest() pins LF and sorts by media_id, but the
# committed copy had last been written CRLF and in another order, so a no-op
# harvester run showed all 1094 lines as changed. Pin LF so the diff is the change.
DybbukMedia/data/media_manifest.tsv text eol=lf
